I've written the plan: session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The command was || true, so the files are on disk for the harness to pick up.

Task 1 — Part of #1068 (product, self-driven, outside `main`): When yoyo's own bash guards refuse a command, the model currently gets a hint telling it to "try a simpler version". The assessment saw this live twice this session. A refusal like that also keeps the whole prompt eligible for auto-retry. The task:
• Collect every refusal message the bash tool can return, by its text. The three the issue names are only a starting list.
• Add those messages to is_deterministic_tool_error, so the hint and the auto-retry treat them like the existing refusals.
• Pin it with a table test on the real messages, near-miss rows (for example command not found must still get the hint), a check that the hint wrapper leaves a refusal unchanged byte for byte, and an atomic positive control.

The issue's second defect (the hard_deny.rs doc wrongly says quoted text counts as one word) stays open on the ticket. That's why the title says "Part of".

Task 2 — Part of #944 (evolve, backlog drain, oldest open issue at 30 days): social.sh (~42 runs a week) will write one spend row per run to the audit-log branch, so the record outlasts the Actions log. Details:
• If a run left no usage record, the row says no_terminal_emit, not 0.
• It can't fail the run: any error prints one line and returns 0, and the main checkout isn't touched.
• Five harness cases run it against a local bare remote.

I grepped evolve.sh's protected list: both files are allowed edits.

